title: '[pallet-revive] Exact pro rata storage deposit refunds'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Closes https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/12692

    Refunds for removed contract storage are now computed as `deposit * removed / stored` with
    exact integer arithmetic, rounded down. Previously the ratio went through `FixedU128`, which
    could refund one unit too little. For example, a contract holding 3 bytes with a byte deposit
    of 3 that removed one byte was refunded 0. It is now refunded 1.

    The netting rule is unchanged and is now documented on `Diff::update_contract` as the
    intended semantics. Within a frame, added and removed bytes and items are offset against
    each other before a rate is applied:

    * A net addition is charged at the current `DepositPerByte` and `DepositPerChildTrieItem`.
    * A net removal is refunded pro rata of the deposit the contract holds, so at the
      contract's average rate. This is not necessarily the rate paid for the removed item.

    After a change of `DepositPerByte` or `DepositPerChildTrieItem` callers observe the
    following. Storage growth is charged at the new rate. Shrinking storage is refunded at the
    contract's average rate, which mixes the old and new rates. Replacing storage with the same
    amount in one frame costs nothing, whether it is a different key or a key that is created
    and deleted again. An in-place overwrite of the same key is netted in `write_raw` and is
    free as before. Deposits already held by contracts are never repriced.

    No migration is needed. The layout of `ContractInfo` is unchanged and recorded deposits stay
    valid.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    Removing contract storage can refund up to one unit more than before for bytes and for
    items, so the storage deposit charged by a call and the storage deposit reported by a dry
    run can be correspondingly lower. Pricing after a change of the deposit rates is otherwise
    unchanged: only net storage growth is charged at the current rate, and net removals are
    refunded at the contract's average rate.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
